From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:08:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: 68k template JIT: virtual calls take the
 template

The polymorphic call path (since 0035) took a call link whose callee
is polymorphicCalleeMask as a polymorphic stub, and assumed the normal
trampoline when the destination was not the closure one. A virtual
call link has the same callee marker, no stub and the virtual call
thunk as its destination: a site that has seen more callees than
maxPolymorphicCallVariantListSize, or a construct site with two
callees that have no call CodeBlock. The stub walk then read from
address 38 and crashed. The destination must now be one of the two
polymorphic trampolines; anything else is the template's, which calls
through the interpreter's own path.

Team 3
---
 Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp b/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp
index 3d4fd8a7026..c79e2a47c2f 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp
@@ -1718,6 +1718,12 @@ private:
         m_hot.loadDisp(0, FunctionRareData::offsetOfExecutable() - static_cast<int>(JSFunction::rareDataTag), 1);
         size_t search2 = m_hot.branch(Builder::Always);
         m_hot.bindBranch(byCallee);
+        // Not the normal trampoline either: a virtual call (no stub; a
+        // construct whose callee has no call CodeBlock, or too many callees),
+        // the template's.
+        uintptr_t normalTrampoline = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(LLInt::getCodePtr<JSEntryPtrTag>(llint_polymorphic_normal_call_trampoline).taggedPtr());
+        m_hot.word(0x0cb9); m_hot.longWord(normalTrampoline); m_hot.longWord(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(linkBase + CallLinkInfo::offsetOfMonomorphicCallDestination())); // cmpi.l #imm,(abs).l
+        slowUnless(Builder::NotEqual);
         m_hot.moveReg(0, 1);
         m_hot.bindBranch(search);
         m_hot.bindBranch(search2);
